Subject: Re: [r-inla] Question about categorial fixed effect interpretation
Message-ID: <NtjP4oRTjR8.SDKVHV_FBwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <NtjP4oRTjR8.eHwhR5rEBwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <NtjP4oRTjR8.eHwhR5rEBwAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/NtjP4oRTjR8/m/SDKVHV_FBwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When using an explicit intercept covariate, the automated factor handling for removing the first level to get contrasts doesn’t work. (That’s also the likely problem you had when having an SPDE model involved)  You wither need to use the full factor and no intercept, or include an intercept but manually convert the factor variable to a set of indicator variables, to ensure identifiability. You can use model.matrix separately on the factor to help with the conversion.

Finn

