I noticed there are a few different ways of extracting the variance and range parameters from a fitted inlabru model. I am getting very different results from them and not sure which one to trust. Note that I do expect a very strong spatial signal here because the model includes some fixed effects that explain a lot of the signal.

1) summary.hyperpar:

mbru$summary.hyperpar

  mean      sd
Precision for the Gaussian observations   1.598   0.148
Range for site                          341.669 800.010
Stdev for site                            0.034   0.032
                                        0.025quant
Precision for the Gaussian observations     1.3286
Range for site                             34.5888
Stdev for site                              0.0027
                                        0.5quant
Precision for the Gaussian observations    1.590
Range for site                           147.486
Stdev for site                             0.024
                                        0.975quant
Precision for the Gaussian observations       1.91
Range for site                             1868.49
Stdev for site                                0.12
                                           mode
Precision for the Gaussian observations  1.5730
Range for site                          61.5183
Stdev for site                           0.0075

2) Using inla.spde2.result

spde.est = INLA::inla.spde2.result(inla = mbru, name = "site",
  spde = spde, do.transf = TRUE)

INLA::inla.zmarginal(spde.est$marginals.variance.nominal[[1]])

Mean            0.105729
Stdev           0.0622142
Quantile  0.025 0.0260214
Quantile  0.25  0.0606892
Quantile  0.5   0.0924807
Quantile  0.75  0.135486
Quantile  0.975 0.262888

INLA::inla.zmarginal(spde.est$marginals.range.nominal[[1]])

Mean            279.088
Stdev           138.287
Quantile  0.025 106.821
Quantile  0.25  182.8
Quantile  0.5   246.473
Quantile  0.75  339.185
Quantile  0.975 637.18

3) Using inlabru::spde.posterior

plot(inlabru::spde.posterior(mbru, "site", what = "variance")) +
  xlim(0,.001)

plot(inlabru::spde.posterior(mbru, "site", what = "range")) +
  xlim(0,1000)

Why are these so different and which one should I trust? Thanks!

